<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="P_Prompt" Revision="3.1" RevisionExtension="01 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2012-07-25T16:53:44.728Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2014-09-03T18:17:54.535Z" EditedBy="PROCESS\Library"
 SoftwareRevision="v18.02" SourceKey="eladdrawdedeer" SourceProtectionType="Full Protection">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Operator Prompt]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details. Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.

This instruction is used to post a prompt (with data, see below)
to an operator and accept operator-input data (see below) and
confirmation.

The configuration data for a set of prompts are stored in a separate
array. An array element of prompt configuration data includes:

*  Prompt message displayed to operator (80-character string)
*  A prompt label (20 characters) for use on prompt list displays
*  Configuration for FOUR response selections (operator chooses
   one of the four buttons), each with:
    - selection label (20 character string)
    - selection enable
    - selection default
*  Configuration for FOUR numeric (REAL) display values, each with:
    - display value label (20 char)
    - display value engineering units (8 char)
    - display value enable
    - value to display (from configuration or AOI input)
    - option to scale displayed value
*  Configuration for FOUR numeric (REAL) operator entries, each with:
    - numeric entry label (20 char)
    - numeric entry engineering units (8 char)
    - entry low and high limits (REAL)
    - option for entry required or not
    - if entry not required, option to use minimum or maximum
       value as entry default
    - option to require operator verify entered value
*  Configuration for FOUR string response operator entries, each with:
    - response label (20 char)
    - response enable
    - option for response entry (non-empty string) required

The prompt response includes the numeric entries, the operator
selection (choice among up to four), and the operator response
string entries.  The number entries are also available as 16-
character text strings for use in building text for reports, etc.
]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
